2026-10-09T18:41:46.5448578Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5548780Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5558953Z [0m
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5559639Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5560176Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5560415Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5561457Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5562441Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5562753Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5563164Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5563571Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5563743Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5564205Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5564755Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5565210Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5565554Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5565714Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5565944Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5566198Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5566464Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5566846Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5566978Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5567094Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5567254Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5567620Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5568124Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5571458Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5571684Z I will:
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5571887Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5572243Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5572986Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5573769Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5574449Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5574900Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5575350Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5575948Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5576342Z    /root
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5587895Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5588657Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5602219Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5603199Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5603664Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5604074Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5604755Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5622331Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5623231Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5633335Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5634351Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5635121Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5635458Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5635748Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5636164Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5636761Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5637672Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5638032Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5638225Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5638701Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5639007Z 
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5639345Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T18:41:46.5639919Z   $ sh ./install-nix
